From 89e7172bfe0ca2e56994fb471334a22e76cb4d58 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?J=C3=B6rg=20Thalheim?= <joerg@thalheim.io>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 14:31:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Accept imported legacy password hashes, upgrade to OPAQUE on
 first bind
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

OPAQUE registration records cannot be derived from existing password
hashes, forcing a password reset for every user when migrating from
another LDAP server.

Instead, allow importing {ARGON2}, {SSHA} and {CRYPT} hashes verbatim
into the password_hash column. During an LDAP simple bind the server
sees the clear-text password, so verify it against the legacy hash and
re-register it as an OPAQUE record on success.

The OPAQUE web login flow never sees the clear-text password; users
must first authenticate through an LDAP bind to trigger the upgrade.

Signed-off-by: Jörg Thalheim <joerg@thalheim.io>
